490
00:17:07,278 --> 00:17:08,518
Isn't it time?

491
00:17:08,778 --> 00:17:09,948
Isn't it time
you accept the fact

492
00:17:10,082 --> 00:17:11,568
that you don't have
what it takes to make it

493
00:17:11,693 --> 00:17:14,024
in the high-pressure world
of dental assisting?

494
00:17:14,207 --> 00:17:15,373
Why don't you
do yourself a favor?

495
00:17:15,498 --> 00:17:16,324
Why don't you
walk out that door

496
00:17:16,438 --> 00:17:18,154
and find something
more your speed, like...

497
00:17:18,536 --> 00:17:21,256
running a hair extension kiosk
at the mall?

498
00:17:22,682 --> 00:17:25,585
You think I'm just
gonna walk out of here?

499
00:17:26,067 --> 00:17:28,553
That I'm just gonna quit
because <i>you</i> told me to?

500
00:17:28,714 --> 00:17:31,196
Well, let me tell you
something about myself--

501
00:17:31,915 --> 00:17:33,092
I...

502
00:17:33,578 --> 00:17:34,811
am a quitter.

503
00:17:34,994 --> 00:17:36,776
A lifelong quitter.

504
00:17:37,108 --> 00:17:38,910
Girl Scouts? Quit.

505
00:17:39,120 --> 00:17:41,087
Piano lessons when they started
with two hands?

506
00:17:41,278 --> 00:17:42,145
Quit.

507
00:17:42,246 --> 00:17:42,898
Working out at Curves?

508
00:17:43,019 --> 00:17:45,332
Quit in the middle of signing up
for the membership.

509
00:17:45,600 --> 00:17:47,657
Every volunteer thing
at my kids' school,

510
00:17:47,790 --> 00:17:48,746
quit, quit, quit.

511
00:17:48,876 --> 00:17:51,393
Oh, and I only got
through 20 "shades of grey."

512
00:17:51,542 --> 00:17:54,373
So if I quit-- and yeah,
I might if it gets too hard--

513
00:17:54,534 --> 00:17:56,300
I'm gonna do it on <i>my</i> terms.

514
00:17:56,453 --> 00:17:57,761
It might be tomorrow.

515
00:17:57,917 --> 00:18:00,574
It might be next week.
It might be the week after!

516
00:18:00,734 --> 00:18:04,928
But definitely not today.

517
00:18:09,263 --> 00:18:10,638
Okay.

518
00:18:11,797 --> 00:18:13,734
Did you see Rick's face?

519
00:18:13,884 --> 00:18:15,626
He totally knew
what this thing was worth.

520
00:18:15,765 --> 00:18:17,719
Of course he did. But we're
gonna have the last laugh

521
00:18:17,858 --> 00:18:19,347
when this thing
is at the Smithsonian,

522
00:18:19,484 --> 00:18:21,558
and we're living in our mansion
in Orson Heights.

523
00:18:21,691 --> 00:18:22,852
(Laughs)

524
00:18:25,128 --> 00:18:26,528
Although...

525
00:18:26,663 --> 00:18:30,360
The L in Gerald kind of
looks more like an R.

526
00:18:30,560 --> 00:18:31,875
And the O in Ford

527
00:18:32,009 --> 00:18:33,851
kind of looks more like a U.

528
00:18:34,426 --> 00:18:37,165
In which case, we have
the 1974 rental car receipt

529
00:18:37,328 --> 00:18:38,816
of some guy named...

530
00:18:38,999 --> 00:18:40,895
Gerard Furd?

531
00:18:42,702 --> 00:18:45,811
Rick, we feel we have
a long-standing

532
00:18:45,961 --> 00:18:47,377
business relationship with you,

533
00:18:47,577 --> 00:18:49,779
and it's not just
about the money, so...

534
00:18:49,897 --> 00:18:51,351
- We'll take the $20.
- Yeah.

535
00:18:51,466 --> 00:18:52,323
I'll give you $10.

536
00:18:52,432 --> 00:18:54,107
- What?
- You offered us $20 before.

537
00:18:54,234 --> 00:18:56,821
- Okay, $9.
- Wait, you can't just <i>lower</i> your offer.

538
00:18:56,958 --> 00:18:59,194
- $7.
- Sell! Sell! Sell!

539
00:18:59,315 --> 00:19:01,246
- All right. All right. All right. We'll
take the $7. - It's Furd, for God sake.

540
00:19:01,558 --> 00:19:02,918
(Register drawer opens)

541
00:19:08,149 --> 00:19:09,995
Oh. Hey.

542
00:19:11,058 --> 00:19:12,160
Hey.

543
00:19:12,733 --> 00:19:13,805
Um...

544
00:19:15,355 --> 00:19:17,401
Look, I know I'm the last person
you wanna see,

545
00:19:17,561 --> 00:19:19,786
but, uh, I just wanted
to let you know

546
00:19:19,904 --> 00:19:22,706
I got a B
on that government test.

547
00:19:22,846 --> 00:19:23,931
Really?

548
00:19:24,093 --> 00:19:26,153
That's great, Axl.
Nice job.

549
00:19:26,280 --> 00:19:27,019
Yeah.

550
00:19:27,159 --> 00:19:28,679
Um, I know things are...

551
00:19:28,996 --> 00:19:32,293
kind of weird between us now
'cause of that... kiss thing.

552
00:19:32,422 --> 00:19:34,686
So I get it if you don't
want to tutor me anymore.

553
00:19:35,002 --> 00:19:36,790
It was lame of me.
(Chuckles nervously)

554
00:19:36,969 --> 00:19:39,154
You hated it.
Sorry and stuff.

555
00:19:39,306 --> 00:19:41,462
Um, so... (Clears throat)
Just to recap...

556
00:19:41,884 --> 00:19:44,170
(Chuckles) Me-- lame. Bye.

557
00:19:44,760 --> 00:19:46,179
I didn't hate it.

558
00:19:48,425 --> 00:19:49,435
You didn't?

559
00:19:49,774 --> 00:19:51,266
No, um...

560
00:19:51,687 --> 00:19:53,555
Actually, it was
kind of pleasant.

561
00:19:54,237 --> 00:19:56,317
But the thing is,
I have a boyfriend.

562
00:19:56,435 --> 00:19:59,243
He's away at college.
So it's moot.

563
00:19:59,467 --> 00:20:01,570
Cool. Cool. Yeah.

564
00:20:01,716 --> 00:20:04,806
Um... uh, yeah. Well...

565
00:20:05,105 --> 00:20:06,748
If you ever break up
with that moot guy,

566
00:20:07,550 --> 00:20:08,753
let me know.

567
00:20:10,833 --> 00:20:11,785
Ow.

568
00:20:12,738 --> 00:20:15,206
<i>Sometimes life knocks us down.</i>

569
00:20:15,840 --> 00:20:17,899
(Pipes groan) <i>Sometimes
it knocks us down a lot.</i>

570
00:20:18,038 --> 00:20:19,970
Okay, there it is.
(Sighs)

571
00:20:20,320 --> 00:20:21,310
I figured out the problem.

572
00:20:21,915 --> 00:20:23,304
The house is broken.

573
00:20:23,823 --> 00:20:24,884
Really?

574
00:20:24,999 --> 00:20:26,065
That's your expert opinion?

575
00:20:26,188 --> 00:20:28,524
Yeah. It's groaning
because it's tired,

576
00:20:28,743 --> 00:20:30,081
much like the people in it.

577
00:20:30,395 --> 00:20:32,507
Oh, see what
you're doing there?

578
00:20:32,663 --> 00:20:33,685
Grinding your teeth.

579
00:20:33,810 --> 00:20:35,934
Your mandibular molars,
to be exact.

580
00:20:36,442 --> 00:20:39,239
Oh, my God.
Mike, I learned something.

581
00:20:39,361 --> 00:20:40,743
I didn't used to
know that before.

582
00:20:41,116 --> 00:20:41,807
Oh!

583
00:20:42,420 --> 00:20:44,313
<i>But there's that</i>
<i>tiny glimmer of hope</i>

584
00:20:44,440 --> 00:20:46,828
<i>that lets us believe</i>
<i>that by some miracle,</i>

585
00:20:46,991 --> 00:20:48,230
<i>it'll all work out.</i>

586
00:20:49,820 --> 00:20:51,026
<i>And then again,</i>

587
00:20:51,151 --> 00:20:54,026
<i>sometimes we just</i>
<i>don't know when to quit.</i>

588
00:21:00,603 --> 00:21:05,000
Sync and corrections by n17t01
www.addic7ed.com

